---
import Layout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PlainSpeakModal from "../components/PlainSpeakModal.astro";
import "../styles/policies.css";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Mind Arc Games">
  <main class="policy-page">
    <div class="policy-shell">
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">Mind Arc Games</p>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">
          Mind Arc Network, Games, and Online Services
        </p>
        <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: August 12, 2026</p>
        <button type="button" class="plain-speak-link" data-plain-speak-open>
          Written under our Plain Speak Doctrine
        </button>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-panel">
        <p>
          Mind Arc Games respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains
          what information we collect, why we collect it, and what happens to it
          when you use the <strong>Mind Arc Network</strong>, our websites,
          games, applications, and online services, including
          <strong>Phoenix Vector: Assault</strong>.
        </p>

        <p>
          Our goal is simple: collect the information we need to operate our
          services without collecting information just for the sake of having
          it.
        </p>

        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

        <p>
          The information we collect depends on which Mind Arc Games services
          you use.
        </p>

        <p>
          When you create or use a Mind Arc Network account, we may collect
          information such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Your email address.</li>
          <li>Your Mind Arc ID (username).</li>
          <li>
            Information needed to sign you in and keep your account secure.
          </li>
          <li>Profile information you choose to add, such as an avatar.</li>
          <li>Game progress and saved game data.</li>
          <li>
            Scores, achievements, statistics, and leaderboard information.
          </li>
          <li>
            Messages, support requests, or feedback you choose to send us.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Our games and website may also provide technical information needed to
          operate, troubleshoot, secure, or improve our services.
        </p>

        <p>
          When we introduce features that collect additional information, we
          will update this policy when appropriate.
        </p>

        <h2>Why We Use Your Information</h2>

        <p>
          We use your information to operate Mind Arc Games and provide the
          features you use.
        </p>

        <p>For example, we may use it to:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Create and manage your Mind Arc Network account.</li>
          <li>Sign you in and confirm that you are the account owner.</li>
          <li>Save your game progress and account data.</li>
          <li>
            Provide online features such as scores, achievements, and
            leaderboards.
          </li>
          <li>Respond when you contact us.</li>
          <li>Find and fix technical problems.</li>
          <li>Improve our games and services.</li>
          <li>
            Protect our users, accounts, games, and services from abuse or
            unauthorized access.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          We do not need to know everything about you to provide our games and
          services, and we do not intend to collect information simply because
          we can.
        </p>

        <h2>Mind Arc Network Accounts</h2>

        <p>
          Your Mind Arc Network account is your account for Mind Arc Games
          online services.
        </p>

        <p>
          As Mind Arc Games grows, the same account may be used across multiple
          Mind Arc Games titles and services. This could include features such
          as saved progress, achievements, scores, leaderboards, cosmetics, and
          other account-based features.
        </p>

        <p>
          When we add new account features that meaningfully change how your
          information is used, we may update this policy.
        </p>

        <h2>Services Provided by Other Companies</h2>

        <p>
          We do not operate every part of our technology ourselves. Mind Arc
          Games uses, or may use, other companies to provide services such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Account authentication and database hosting.</li>
          <li>Website and cloud hosting.</li>
          <li>Email delivery.</li>
          <li>Game distribution.</li>
          <li>Payments.</li>
          <li>Analytics and diagnostics.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          These companies may receive or process information when necessary to
          provide their services.
        </p>

        <p>
          For example, Mind Arc Games currently uses Supabase for parts of the
          Mind Arc Network account and database system.
        </p>

        <p>
          Other platforms, such as Google Play, Apple's App Store, or Steam, may
          also process information when you use their services. Their own
          privacy policies apply to information they collect directly through
          their platforms.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and Browser Data</h2>

        <p>
          Our website uses cookies and similar browser technologies for features
          such as account authentication and maintaining your signed-in session.
        </p>

        <p>
          Some cookies are necessary for these features to work. For example, if
          your browser cannot maintain the information needed for your account
          session, you may be signed out.
        </p>

        <p>
          We explain what cookies are and how Mind Arc Games uses them in our
          <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          If we introduce optional technologies such as certain analytics or
          advertising systems, we will update our policies and provide
          additional choices when required.
        </p>

        <h2>How We Protect Your Information</h2>

        <p>
          We take reasonable steps to protect the information entrusted to us.
        </p>

        <p>
          That includes using security measures designed to prevent unauthorized
          access, alteration, disclosure, or loss of account information.
        </p>

        <p>
          No website, database, or Internet connection can be guaranteed to be
          completely secure. We cannot promise that a security problem will
          never happen, but protecting user information is an important part of
          operating our services.
        </p>

        <h2>How Long We Keep Information</h2>

        <p>
          We keep information for as long as we reasonably need it to provide
          our services, maintain accounts, meet legal requirements, resolve
          disputes, prevent fraud or abuse, and protect Mind Arc Games and its
          users.
        </p>

        <p>
          Different types of information may need to be kept for different
          lengths of time.
        </p>

        <p>
          When information is no longer reasonably needed, we may delete or
          anonymize it.
        </p>

        <h2>Your Choices</h2>

        <p>
          You may contact us if you have questions about information associated
          with your Mind Arc Network account or want to request that your
          account be deleted.
        </p>

        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may also have legal rights concerning
          your personal information.
        </p>

        <p>
          Some information may need to be kept after an account is deleted when
          required by law or when reasonably necessary for matters such as
          security, fraud prevention, or resolving disputes.
        </p>

        <p>
          Deleting your account may permanently remove access to information
          connected to that account, including saved progress or other
          account-based features.
        </p>

        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

        <p>
          Mind Arc Games does not knowingly collect personal information from
          children in violation of applicable privacy laws.
        </p>

        <p>
          Age and parental-consent requirements are different around the world.
          Where the law requires parental or guardian permission for a child to
          use a service, that permission must be obtained.
        </p>

        <p>
          If we learn that personal information was collected from a child in a
          way that does not comply with applicable law, we will take appropriate
          steps to address it.
        </p>

        <h2>International Users</h2>

        <p>
          Mind Arc Games is available through the Internet, which means our
          users and the companies that help operate our services may be located
          in different countries.
        </p>

        <p>
          As a result, information may sometimes be stored or processed outside
          the country where you live.
        </p>

        <p>
          We take reasonable steps to protect personal information when it is
          processed as part of our services.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>

        <p>
          Mind Arc Games will continue to change as we build new games, account
          features, and online services. That may occasionally require us to
          update this Privacy Policy.
        </p>

        <p>
          When we make changes, we will update the
          <strong>Last Updated</strong> date at the top of this page. If a change
          is important enough that additional notice is appropriate or legally required,
          we will provide it.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact Us</h2>

        <p>
          Questions about this Privacy Policy or information associated with
          your Mind Arc Network account are welcome.
        </p>

        <div class="contact-card">
          <p><strong>Mind Arc Games</strong></p>

          <p>
            Email:
            <a href="mailto:contact@mindarcgames.com">
              contact@mindarcgames.com
            </a>
          </p>

          <p>
            Website:
            <a
              href="https://mindarcgames.com"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              mindarcgames.com
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <PlainSpeakModal />
</Layout>